.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (3, 1)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>embedding</th></tr><tr><td>array[f32, 2]</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>[-3.434997, -0.106764]</td></tr><tr><td>[3.194072, 2.138245]</td></tr><tr><td>[1.460992, -1.859551]</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


A `List` column works too, as long as every row has the same length:

::: {#2299d2e2 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
as_list = df.with_columns(pl.col("embedding").arr.to_list())
as_list.select(pl.col("embedding").umap.fit_transform(random_state=0)).head(3)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (3, 1)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>embedding</th></tr><tr><td>array[f32, 2]</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>[-3.434997, -0.106764]</td></tr><tr><td>[3.194072, 2.138245]</td></tr><tr><td>[1.460992, -1.859551]</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


Lists of different lengths raise an error, because UMAP needs every vector to have the same
dimensionality.

### Several numeric columns

Pass several numeric columns to `pu.umap()` and they're stacked into a feature matrix, like `X` in
scikit-learn:

::: {#07d24dcd .cell execution_count=4}
``` {.python .cell-code}
wide = pl.DataFrame(vectors, schema=[f"feature_{i}" for i in range(8)])
wide.select(pu.umap("feature_0", "feature_1", "feature_2", random_state=0)).head(3)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
